export function companyPage() {
    return `${heading('About Valtron', 'Valtron Forge &amp; Fittings', 'Manufacturers and exporters of stainless steel flanges and pipe fittings, based in Mumbai.')}
<section class="vf-wrap vf-company"><img src="img/flange%20banner01.jpg" alt="Collection of machined flanges with different hubs, bores and bolt patterns" width="1024" height="576"><div><p class="vf-eyebrow">Our company</p><h2>Building on a stainless steel legacy</h2><p>Valtron Forge &amp; Fittings was founded by Jitendra Kumar as a sister concern of Rishabh Forge Fittings &amp; Mfg. Co., a Mumbai business specialising in stainless steel flanges and fittings.</p><p>Rishabh Forge Fittings &amp; Mfg. Co. brings a legacy spanning over 35 years, as described in our company catalogue. Building on this foundation, Valtron continues the focus on quality, reliability and stainless steel solutions for industrial requirements.</p><p>Our expertise is in stainless steel flanges and fittings that combine strength, durability and precision. Our understanding of customer requirements supports customised solutions for different applications, with flanges at the centre of our range and buttweld and forged fittings for supporting pipework.</p>${button('contact.html', 'Contact the Team')}</div></section>
<section class="vf-section vf-about-soft" id="about-range"><div class="vf-wrap"><div class="vf-about-heading"><p class="vf-eyebrow">What we offer</p><h2>A range organised around the connection.</h2><p>Flange selection starts with the joint, not just a product name. The connection type, facing, bore, material and pressure-temperature basis all need to work together.</p></div><div class="vf-about-columns"><div><h3>Pipe flange connections</h3><p>Weld-neck, slip-on, socket-weld, threaded and lap-joint forms support different pipe joining and assembly requirements. Our product pages outline the information needed to distinguish one connection from another.</p><a class="vf-text-link" href="flanges.html">Browse flange types ${arrow}</a></div><div><h3>Equipment &amp; special forms</h3><p>Blind, long weld-neck, orifice and other flange configurations address closure, equipment and measurement interfaces. Non-standard details need a drawing number, revision and clear mating dimensions before a requirement can be reviewed.</p><a class="vf-text-link" href="flange-types-guide.html">Explore connection selection ${arrow}</a></div><div><h3>Materials &amp; mating faces</h3><p>Material guides and facing references help define the enquiry, from carbon and stainless steels to project-specified alloys. They are a starting point for discussion, not confirmation that a grade is suitable for every service.</p><a class="vf-text-link" href="flange-materials.html">View material references ${arrow}</a></div></div><p class="vf-about-supporting">For supporting pipework: <a href="buttweld-fittings.html">Buttweld Fittings</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> <a href="forged.html">Forged Fittings</a>. Specify the fitting geometry, end connection and applicable standard with your enquiry.</p></div></section>
<section class="vf-section" id="about-approach"><div class="vf-wrap vf-about-split"><div><p class="vf-eyebrow">Our vision</p><h2>Growing through quality and innovation.</h2><p>Our vision is to reach new markets while maintaining high standards of quality and innovation. We aim to explore new possibilities in stainless steel manufacturing and make a lasting contribution to the global industry.</p><h3>Our expertise</h3><p>We specialise in stainless steel flanges and fittings, bringing together product knowledge, precision and an understanding of the market. Customised solutions are developed around the varied requirements of our clients.</p></div><div class="vf-about-principles"><h3>Why choose us?</h3><div><h3>Innovation and excellence</h3><p>Continuous improvement guides our approach to stainless steel solutions, with attention to product quality and the evolving needs of industrial applications.</p></div><div><h3>Speed and efficiency</h3><p>We value our customers' time and focus on responsive coordination and efficient delivery planning to help keep projects on track. Delivery schedules are agreed for each order.</p></div><div><h3>Dynamic growth</h3><p>Our catalogue describes a growing company powered by a young, forward-looking team. Agility and fresh perspectives support our approach to new requirements and opportunities.</p></div><div><h3>Customer-centric approach</h3><p>We believe in building long-term relationships through customised solutions and responsive support that address the individual needs of every client.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="vf-section vf-about-soft" id="about-facilities"><div class="vf-wrap"><div class="vf-about-heading"><p class="vf-eyebrow">Inside Valtron</p><h2>People, facilities and work on the shop floor.</h2><p>Our company catalogue presents the Valtron team, Unit 1 and Unit 2, together with photographs of forming, machining and flange preparation. The factory gallery brings these views together in one place.</p></div><div class="vf-about-photos"><figure><a href="gallery.html"><img src="img/gallery/team.png" alt="Valtron team gathered inside the factory beneath the company banner" width="704" height="400" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>The Valtron team, as shown in our company catalogue.</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="gallery.html"><img src="img/gallery/unit-one.png" alt="Exterior of the Valtron Unit 1 factory with staff at the entrance" width="579" height="385" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Unit 1: a view from the catalogue's factory photographs.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="vf-about-facility-links"><p>For a particular order, confirm the manufacturing route, inspection arrangements and any facility-approval requirements with the team.</p><a class="vf-text-link" href="gallery.html">Visit the factory gallery ${arrow}</a></div></div></section>
<section class="vf-section" id="about-quality"><div class="vf-wrap vf-about-split"><div><p class="vf-eyebrow">Quality requirements</p><h2>Define the evidence alongside the product.</h2><p>A flange requirement includes more than dimensions. The material specification, inspection scope and records requested by the project are part of defining a complete order.</p><p>Documentation and testing requirements should be agreed before supply. Certificates, third-party inspection and sector-specific approvals are not assumed to be included unless confirmed for the order.</p><a class="vf-text-link" href="flange-standards.html">Review flange standards ${arrow}</a></div><dl class="vf-about-quality-list"><dt>Material identity &amp; traceability</dt><dd>State the grade, product specification and certificate requirements. Identify any heat-number traceability or marking expectations in the purchase specification.</dd><dt>Dimensions &amp; joint interfaces</dt><dd>Confirm the applicable standard and edition, flange type, bore, bolt pattern, facing and required finish. Drawing-based details need an approved revision.</dd><dt>Inspection &amp; test scope</dt><dd>List the required checks, acceptance criteria and witness or hold points. Special testing and third-party involvement must be discussed before confirmation.</dd><dt>Protection &amp; delivery records</dt><dd>Include packing, face protection, identification and dispatch-document requirements so the delivery can be checked against the agreed order.</dd></dl></div></section>
<section class="vf-section vf-about-soft" id="about-enquiry"><div class="vf-wrap"><div class="vf-about-heading"><p class="vf-eyebrow">Working with us</p><h2>From your specification to a defined enquiry.</h2><p>Whether you are planning an installation or replacing an existing component, a few clear details make the first conversation more useful.</p></div><ol class="vf-about-steps"><li><h3>Share the requirement</h3><p>Send the flange type, size, material, rating, standard and quantity. For a replacement, include the mating details rather than relying only on a photograph.</p></li><li><h3>Resolve the details</h3><p>Provide drawings and revisions where needed. Confirm inspection records, special conditions and any customer approvals that affect the scope.</p></li><li><h3>Agree the supply scope</h3><p>Discuss availability, delivery location and schedule with the team. Technical requirements and commercial terms are confirmed for the individual order.</p></li></ol><div class="vf-about-facility-links"><p>Our Services page covers industry-specific enquiry considerations, including process plants, marine systems and energy facilities.</p><a class="vf-text-link" href="service.html">Industries we serve ${arrow}</a></div></div></section>
<section class="vf-section" id="about-contact"><div class="vf-wrap vf-about-split"><div><p class="vf-eyebrow">Speak with our team</p><h2>Your point of contact in Mumbai.</h2><p>Send your requirement by email or begin a product enquiry through the contact page. Drawings can be shared by email or in the WhatsApp conversation after the initial enquiry.</p><p>Include your company name, contact details and any target delivery date so the conversation can start with the right context.</p>${button('contact.html', 'Discuss Your Requirement')}</div><div class="vf-about-contact"><h3>Valtron Forge &amp; Fittings</h3><address>12/13 Badrika Ashram Building, 1st Khetwadi,<br>Near Alankar Cinema, Girgaon,<br>Mumbai, Maharashtra 400004, India</address><a href="mailto:sales@valtronforge.com"><i class="far fa-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i> sales@valtronforge.com</a><a href="tel:+919619770076"><i class="fas fa-phone-alt" aria-hidden="true"></i> +91 96197 70076</a><a href="Valtron%20Forge_0222.pdf" download="Valtron-Forge-Catalogue.pdf"><i class="fas fa-file-download" aria-hidden="true"></i> Download Catalogue (PDF)</a></div></div></section>${browseLinks()}`;
}

